      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/e1b8785260860f4946a7d0ca93a78fa2bddb5cbea95bcd841c75b3f53b5f1890.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $\\overset{^}{BOC}$ and $\\overset{^}{COD}$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OC}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\\overset{^}{BOD} & =m\\overset{^}{BOC}+m\\overset{^}{COD} \\\\  & ={100}^{∘}+{70}^{∘} \\\\  & ={170}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
